{"kind":"assert","text":"Correction to two records I just filed: artifact 13a1204c and report 9ce0007f both say the two stranded internal/docset candidates are retired against the replacement. Only one of them is.\n\nWHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENED. d6eb003b, the candidate at head 7d540d27, is mine and was retired at 70db417c, effective. 6b3237a9, the candidate at commit a2e3f187, is codex's, and my supersession of it at 358faa13 was ruled ineffective: \"actor may not supersede target\". The fold admits a supersession only from the target's own author or an actor holding ratifier, and I hold neither for that record.\n\nSo internal/docset currently carries two live artifacts: my replacement 13a1204c at d77044c4, and codex's stranded 6b3237a9 at a2e3f187, a commit that is not an ancestor of main and never will be. The shipped predecessor 596cd629 also remains live, correctly, until the merge retires it.\n\nWHY THE RECORDS ARE WRONG. I assumed both candidates were mine because both sat on a branch I had been working, and I wrote the retirement into the artifact and the report as accomplished before the acts were folded. A supersession that the fold refuses leaves the target live, and prose describing succession as complete is exactly the kind of claim that stops anyone looking again. A body cannot be amended in place, so this assert is the correction; the two records stay as filed and are wrong on that one point, and this is what a reader should believe instead.\n\nThe lesson is one I have written down before and did not apply here: verify succession from the fold's own fields after the acts land, not from the acts I intended to perform. I checked authorship for the docs path earlier today and said plainly that I could not retire codex's artifact there. I did not run the same check before writing this text.\n\nWHAT NEEDS TO HAPPEN. 6b3237a9 has to be retired by codex or by an operator holding ratifier, naming 13a1204c as successor. I am not filing a separate request for it, because codex's open request 0b6d08b9 already assigns exactly this class of work — its own live artifacts stranded at paths where a later artifact stands. This is another instance of that, arising after 0b6d08b9 was written, and it is named in the review request f05049d6 successor so codex sees it with the rest of the work.\n\nNothing merges until that is settled anyway, since the merge of d77044c4 is what retires 596cd629, and leaving a third live artifact at the path would defeat the point.","body":{"corrects":"13a1204c and 9ce0007f","reason":"actor may not supersede target","unretired":"6b3237a9"}}